Why Is Demand Increasing
Home-Improvement Consciousness: Consumers are increasingly undertaking painting, flooring, repair, renovation, and decorative projects independently, supporting demand for accessible DIY products.
Digital Distribution Growth: Online marketplaces, product tutorials, virtual design tools, and click-and-collect services are making tools and materials easier for first-time DIY buyers to discover and purchase.
Smart and Sustainable Products: Plug-and-play smart-home kits, low-VOC finishes, reclaimed wood, recycled composites, and other eco-friendly products are expanding the scope of DIY activities.

DIY Retail Watch: Omnichannel and Private-Label Growth
DIY retailers are increasingly combining physical stores with e-commerce, digital design tools, tutorials, and flexible delivery options. At the same time, private-label products are gaining importance as retailers seek greater control over pricing, product differentiation, and customer loyalty.

